      "message": "As a general comment, why not trying to factorize into an inline wrapper method these WALT specific bits. IMO, something like this:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_WALT\nstatic inline int\nrequested_capacity(struct sched_capacity_reqs *scr)\n{\n        if (!walt_disabled \u0026\u0026 sysctl_sched_use_walt_cpu_util)\n                return scr-\u003ecfs;\n        return scr-\u003ecfs + scr-\u003ert;\n}\n#else\n#define requested_capacity(scr) (scr-\u003ecfs + scr-\u003ert)\n#endif\n\nit helps in keeping a more streamlined code at the caller side with the previous #ifdef/if/else \"confusing\" code becoming just a simpler:\n\n        new_capacity \u003d requested_capacity(scr);\n\nThus making a bit less confusing the definition of update_cpu_capacity_request()",
